The item at index n of a list, counting from 0. The input is the pair [n xs]. The output is [0 item] when there is one, and [1 message] when the index is past the end.
---

---
(fn p
  (letrec nth
    (fn (n l)
      (if (? l) [1 "index out of range"] (if (= n 0) [0 (head l)] (nth (- n 1) (tail l)))))
    (nth (head p) (tail p))))
---
[0 7 8 9 ~] => [0 7] fuel 100000
[2 7 8 9 ~] => [0 9] fuel 100000
[3 7 8 9 ~] => [1 "index out of range"] fuel 100000
[0 ~] => [1 "index out of range"] fuel 100000
